<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Local perception sensors: Artery's reference arrangement, which carries the geometry that
  ETSI TR 103 562 V2.1.1 Table 4 records.

  Four radars, a short-range and a long-range pair, mirrored front and rear:

      short range:  65 m, field of view +-40 degrees   (fovAngle 80)
      long range:  150 m, field of view  +-5 degrees   (fovAngle 10)

  Those two pairs of numbers are exactly Table 4's configuration 1, and exactly what
  artery/scenarios/artery/omnetpp.ini configures. The TR's clause 5.3.2.2 states the study used
  Artery's own environment model, and Table 4 sits in clause 5.3.3.2, which describes the ns-3
  port of those same sensors - which is why the table labels the pair "Forward sensors" while
  Artery mirrors them to the rear. We follow Artery.

  Not used: Table 4's configuration 2 (150 m, 360 degrees). Clause 5.3.2.2 calls it "an artificial
  setup ... to be able to generate large CP messages in specific scenarios".

  Ranges and apertures are set per sensor name in omnetpp.ini, and must stay in step with
  Noise.sensorCoverage there.
-->
<sensors>
    <sensor name="FrontShortRangeRadar" type="artery.envmod.sensor.FrontRadar" />
    <sensor name="FrontLongRangeRadar"  type="artery.envmod.sensor.FrontRadar" />
    <sensor name="RearShortRangeRadar"  type="artery.envmod.sensor.RearRadar" />
    <sensor name="RearLongRangeRadar"   type="artery.envmod.sensor.RearRadar" />
</sensors>
